  "entry": "code/index.html",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load a network file, draw it with a force-directed or no-overlap layout, compute its global properties (density, average degree, clustering, shortest path, diameter, global efficiency) and per-vertex degree, clustering and centrality, then export the graph or a properties report. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
